{title: Away in a Manger}
{artist: Anonymous & James R. Murray}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
A[F]way in a manger, no [Bb]crib for a bed,
the [C]little Lord [F]Jesus laid [C]down his sweet [F]head;
the stars in the sky looked [Bb]down where he lay,
the [C]little Lord [F]Jesus, a[C]sleep on the [F]hay.

Verse 2
[F]The cattle are lowing, [Bb]the Baby awakes,
But [C]little Lord [F]Jesus, [C]no crying He [F]makes;
I love Thee, Lord Jesus, [Bb]look down from the sky
And [C]stay by [F]my [C]cradle til morning is [F]nigh.

Verse 3
[F]Be near me, Lord Jesus, I [Bb]ask Thee to stay
Close [C]by me [F]for ever, and [C]love me, I [F]pray;
Bless all the dear children [Bb]in Thy tender care,
And [C]fit us for [F]Heaven [C]to live with Thee [F]there.
